  "definition": "A ground station is the terrestrial radio or optical facility that communicates with a spacecraft. It provides telemetry, tracking and command, often abbreviated **TT&C**, and may also receive payload data. The station is one part of the wider ground segment, which includes mission-control systems, networks, storage, processing, user terminals and operations staff.[^1]",
